WEBVTT

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.710
The internal security here is a total joke!

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.620
All right! I'm lovely today, too! If I may say
so myself, I'm just too cute for a germ!

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.210
And how adorable!

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.790
There's no Immune Cell that could possibly
attack such an adorable germ like me!

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.460
When I catch him off guard with my cuteness,
I'm going to go, "Blam! Pow!"

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.330
It's like I've taken over this body!

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.170
Die, you damn germ!

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.000
"WHITE BLOOD CELL"

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.210
This is the inside of a human body.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.790
Hello, Macrophage!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.460
Oh my!

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.000
Good afternoon!

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:06.330
"FRAGILE"
"CONDENSED GAS"

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.290
"FRAGILE"
"CONDENSED GAS"
I see that you're full of energy today, too.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.290
"FRAGILE"
"CONDENSED GAS"
Thank you very much!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.500
"FRAGILE"
"CONDENSED GAS"
And I see that you're working hard
as a good senpai!

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.080
No, I wouldn't go that far!
No, really, seriously--

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.710
You're in the way! What are you doing,
wandering around like this? Are you lost again?

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.880
I'm so sorry, Killer T Cell.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.000
♪ We're the invincible T Cells! ♪

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.670
Are you okay, Senpai?

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.750
Hey, I'm fine!

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:41.710
"ARTERY"

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.750
"ARTERY"
Roughly 37 trillion cells are working energetically
and with all their might again today.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:50.210
Roughly 37 trillion cells are working energetically
and with all their might again today.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.750
"EPISODE 1:
BUMP"

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.290
"EPISODE 1:
BUMP"
"Bump."

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.290
"EPISODE 1:
BUMP"

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:08.750
Th-Th-Th-Thank you... for waiting!

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.120
"CELL"
Th-Th-Th-Thank you... for waiting!

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.420
"CELL"
I've come to deliver your nutrients and oxygen!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.210
"CELL"
Hey, I appreciate your hard work.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.000
"CELL"

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:17.960
Thank you very much!

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.670
"STING STING"
Thank you very much!

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:25.040
S-Sorry about making you come
through such cramped quarters.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.210
Oh no! It's my job!

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.540
Y-Your face is all scraped up,
so take care, okay?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.460
All righty.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.920
Hey, look who showed up here
but Red Blood Cell!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.040
Hey! I know you!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.460
You're White Blood Cell's friend!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.540
Hey there!

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.880
Listen, I hope you don't mind my asking,
but have you seen 1146?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.460
Now that you mention it,
I haven't seen him in a while.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.040
Are you looking for him?

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:56.830
Yeah. He's been pretty slammed
with work lately,

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:00.580
so I'm worried that he might be
feeling run-down or in a foul mood.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.580
I thought I'd ask him to go for tea
and calm him down!

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.040
Is that right? Sounds good to me!

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.500
Well, hey, I'm embarrassed
to sound so patronizing, you know!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.170
Don't give it another thought!

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:17.290
Hey, but maybe there's no need
for you to be so worried.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.880
The last time I saw him, he was taking it easy,
sipping on some yummy-looking germ soup!

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.750
"GERM SOUP"
The last time I saw him, he was taking it easy,
sipping on some yummy-looking germ soup!

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.460
I think he might be better
at switching gears than we think.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.830
You know how grounded White Blood Cell is!
I'm sure he's taking care of himself just fine!

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.750
4989?

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.500
Sorry.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.330
It's just that I had no idea there were any
Red Blood Cells looking out for us like that.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:46.420
I mean, I never even dreamed it!

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.830
I was so moved, I just broke down into tears!

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.040
Hey, come on! You're embarrassing me!

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:57.670
"RELAXING TEA"
Knowing how grounded White Blood Cell is,
I bet he's sipping tea right now, looking like this!

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.120
"RELAXING TEA"
"THIS TEA IS SO GOOD"

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.330
"RELAXING TEA"
"THIS TEA IS SO GOOD"
This tea is so good!

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.380
I think you're right!

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.580
You're not getting away!

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.460
W-W-W-Wait! Take a good look!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.960
How dare you assault a lovely germ like me!

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.250
This White Blood Cell...

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.830
...is bonkers!

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.170
His deadly accuracy at top speed,

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.920
those devastating attacks that seem
to be cutting off all worldly desires...

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.250
He's my enemy, but I applaud him!

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.670
This is U-1146 of the White
Blood Cell Neutrophil Division.

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.790
The invading Bacteria have been exterminated.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.880
No matter what kind of germ it is,
it will be obliterated without mercy.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.290
That's our job.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:47.620
We can't let even a single one
slip through the cracks.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.420
No matter what!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.830
S-So sorry! I guess
I got in your way, didn't I?

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.790
Hey! No, not at all!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.710
I should be apologizing for scaring you.
I'll clean this up right away and leave.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.040
Oh no, that's all right!

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.670
The thing is, I'm training
to become a strong Platelet right now.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:16.080
I can't put this down
under any circumstances!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.920
Huh? Training?

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.000
Would you mind tossing that
coagulation factor my way, please?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.500
So I can catch it!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.620
Uh, sure. I don't mind at all.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:26.540
Can you handle it?

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.580
Thank you so much!

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.960
I'll be fine!

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.540
All right.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.830
Here!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.500
"STUMBLE STUMBLE"

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.290
"BAM'

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.330
Hey!

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.670
"PLOP"
Plop!

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.620
Are you okay?

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.040
Plop...

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.710
Looks just like her!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:47.540
--I-I'm all right. I'm so sorry to worry you.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:52.380
--She's fighting back tears!
I'll pick those up for you now, okay?
--I-I'm all right. I'm so sorry to worry you.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.460
Still, this is a White Blood Cell
migration route, you know?

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.880
Did you lose your way
during training, maybe?

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.420
"BLUSH BLUSH"

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.830
"BLUSH BLUSH"
Just like her.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.330
"PLATELETS"

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.380
I don't usually see you alone like this.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.750
What happened? Did you get into a fight
with that kid you're always with?

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.880
--Th-That's not it at all!
Leader is such a kind girl!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.170
--You see, you see...
--Th-That's not it at all!
Leader is such a kind girl!

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:18.210
It's just that I'm so weak.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.170
The other day...

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:26.710
...when we were practicing primary
blood clotting inside the bone marrow...

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.120
Are you okay?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.960
"PLOP"
Plop!

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:36.420
Are you all right? Leader? Backward Cap?

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:39.120
So, they call you Backward Cap, huh?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.920
Since we're so tiny, at work, we clump together
to make up for our lack of height.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:51.040
And there's nothing more important
than working as one...

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.250
But since I'm twice as weak
as the next Platelet,

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.250
I was always dragging everyone else down.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.960
Even so, everyone still kept
cheering me on, but...

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.750
So, I come to check on my apprentices...

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.830
...and what exactly is this I'm seeing?

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:08.120
"SNACK"

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:09.620
"SNACK"
Th-That voice!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.290
M-Master!

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:15.620
Who would've thought

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:21.210
that among my apprentices, I'd still find
an underdeveloped useless kid like you?

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:25.040
Out there in the real world,
"I can't do it" just won't cut it!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.080
Make sure you've whipped yourself
into shape by the next hemorrhage!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.120
Okay!

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.670
What I want is strength!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.500
That's why I'm carrying twice
the normal load of coagulation factors...

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.500
...to get myself into shape! I-It's so heavy!

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.120
"TREMBLE TREMBLE"
...to get myself into shape! I-It's so heavy!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:41.250
"CLENCH"
"TREMBLE TREMBLE"
...to get myself into shape! I-It's so heavy!

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:44.880
"CLENCH"
"TREMBLE TREMBLE"
I see. I really hope you can become stronger!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.620
But...

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:51.250
She yelled at me,
but Master's absolutely right.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:56.290
I might end up thwarting the others
during a real mission because I'm incompetent.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:02.960
So, I've made up my mind
not to go back until I've gotten stronger.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.790
Is that right?

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:09.250
Well, but there's no need to panic, right?

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.750
Backward Cap, you have the positive mindset
to work hard at it, don't you?

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.880
As long as there's one of you like that,

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.420
it'll inspire the others to follow suit,
and then you can all do a great job.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.210
There's no way that
you'd be thwarting them...

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:29.210
...so why don't you go on back
and see how training together works out?

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:31.210
You really think so?

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:33.290
I see!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.580
Look, we're close to the epidermis now.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:43.920
Oh, wow!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:47.380
This is the main road
along the temporal vein!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:51.880
Hey! White Blood Cell!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.290
Hey, long time no see!

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.670
Hey, Red Blood Cell!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:00.000
Oh, it's Platelet's friend.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.960
This is Backward Cap.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.290
Hello, Backward Cap!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.790
Hello!

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:12.380
What a coincidence! Just a minute ago,
we were wondering how you were doing--

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.500
What the cell's going on?
An external injury? Where's the wound?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:23.620
Every capillary vein in the area is ruptured!

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.750
Red Blood Cell!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.290
Don't worry about me!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.580
White Blood Cell...

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.170
Take Backward Cap!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.830
Gotcha!

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.920
Please give it all you've got!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.290
Will she be all right?

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.750
Yeah. No need to worry.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.540
She's sure toughened up!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.040
No. 1146!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.330
So, this is where you've been
all this time, huh?

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:54.670
Hey, No. 4989, are we under attack?
This is an attack, right?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.330
Hold up, No. 1146. Haven't you noticed?

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.120
This isn't like any of the other times.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:02.830
The blood cells should be flying
out of the wound, but look!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.880
It's like we've been thrown into
some kind of zero gravity space!

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.380
What the...

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.040
I see!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.460
That's right!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.880
This means that there's no wound!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.880
And this is the head area!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.330
So, this must be...

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.460
...a bump, then?

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:20.920
Bump.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:21.750
A lump-like protrusion caused by swelling
and bleeding on the outer skull.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:27.710
"BUMP"
A lump-like protrusion caused by swelling
and bleeding on the outer skull.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.830
Stop the internal bleeding...

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:36.750
"GRIP"

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:37.120
"GRIP"
Looks like it's time for me to step up!

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.830
Looks like it's time for me to step up!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:41.750
That's what I like to hear!

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.290
Give it your all, Backward Cap!

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.830
Right!

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:49.580
I'll do my best!

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.920
And as for us Neutrophils...

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.880
No. 4989! You ready?

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.460
Yeah! I know what to do!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.170
Internal bleeding is a hemorrhage
occurring under the skin.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:05.790
Which means that there's no wound that can
serve as a pathway for enemy intruders.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.170
In other words...

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.790
...what we can do as Neutrophils is...

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.380
...nothing.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:15.880
All right! Let's work hard
at our jobs today, too!

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.170
Okay!

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.080
<i>Cells at Work!!</i>

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.210
<i>Cells at Work!!</i>

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:31.880
All right, everybody, listen up!

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:36.120
This is internal bleeding,
but it's the same job as always.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:40.040
We're going to assemble in the ruptured area,
form a primary blood clot,

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.790
then form a secondary blood clot by sticking the
Red and White Blood Cells together with fibrin,

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.380
to stop the bleeding!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.290
We have a wide area to cover,
so it won't be easy, but let's do our best!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.960
Okay!

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.080
There's damage here, too!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.420
Anyone who's free, please come over here!

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.920
It's clotted!

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.000
We can cast the fibrin now!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.670
Please bring us the coagulation factors!

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.880
Okay!

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.460
The coagulation factor!

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:11.000
Backward Cap, you have
a really great attitude!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.000
She's right! Good for you, Backward Cap!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.210
It's not about whether you're strong or not!
Sometimes a good attitude's all you need!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.790
Bad news, everybody! Listen, listen!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.080
We don't have enough coagulation factors!

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:26.620
Don't worry! Backward Cap's on it--

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.830
Listen, listen! It's not that!

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.000
The really bad news we're talking about is...

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.540
Look at that!

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:35.830
That's...

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.670
Sorry!

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:41.380
The damaged area is too big
for us to close up, right?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.500
What should we do?

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:46.460
Looks like we'll have to assemble far and wide
and close the whole thing off at once.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.750
Everybody, gather round!

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:50.750
We're going to join forces
and form a primary blood clot together!

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.670
Come on, you, too, Backward Cap, hurry!

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:57.290
Uh-oh! Primary blood clots are what
Backward Cap has trouble with! Jeez!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.580
Y-You can do it, Backward Cap!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.330
Who's Backward Cap?

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:02.380
"PLOP"
Plop!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.000
I see, so this gives you trouble, Backward Cap!
Wh-What should we do?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.460
Is there anyone who can
take Backward Cap's place?

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:11.290
Hold on a second!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:15.120
Primary blood clot... We all need to unite
and work as one right now, but I...

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:15.790
"BONK"
Primary blood clot... We all need to unite
and work as one right now, but I...

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:19.580
"BONK"
If I'm like this, I'm going to
throw everyone else off, too!

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.210
What the cell are you doing?

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.710
Lackadaisical! No motivation whatsoever!

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.580
"MEGAKARYOCYTE"
What a bunch of slackers! Asleep at the wheel!

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.420
What a bunch of slackers! Asleep at the wheel!

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.500
Little squirts!

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.080
Megakaryocyte.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.960
The cell that produces Platelets.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:40.710
The largest of all the cells in the bone marrow.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.830
--Master Megakaryocyte!
--Master!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.460
So, I'm worried and come to check
on you, and what do I find?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.420
Seriously, you call yourselves my apprentices?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.710
I know I taught you!

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.000
That since there aren't much in the
way of defensive barriers like muscles

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.670
or fat on the skull, the veins are
easily ruptured by external trauma!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:58.670
That because of all the capillaries,
bleeding there leads to catastrophe!

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:01.380
That it's dangerous when the internal bleeding
can't be stopped! Remember?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.000
W-We're very sorry, Master!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:06.670
That's not the way to go, Megakaryocyte!

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.670
Putting pressure on Backward Cap now
will only backfire in the end!

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.960
Ugh, the wind's smothering my voice!

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:15.120
I said, who is this Backward Cap anyway?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.000
Just look at that!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.830
Thanks to that tongue-lashing,
she's curled up into a ball!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:20.960
I don't get it!

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.380
To me, it just seems like she's only yelling
because it makes her feel good.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.460
But could it be

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:31.210
that she has the ability to bring the
Platelets together and resolve this issue?

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.460
Does she actually have a plan?

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:34.960
All right.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:39.670
Now, how can I goad
these useless brats into action?

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.170
Okay, I've got it.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:43.170
"WHOOSH"

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.880
"WHOOSH"
Listen up, little ones!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.210
Ready?

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:52.830
Whoever does the best job today...

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:58.210
...will get this special "You Did a Great Job
as a Platelet / Good Kid" gold medal!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.000
"WOW"

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.580
I'm going to try harder!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.540
Get to it!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.420
--A medal!
--A medal!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.170
A gold medal!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.920
She's bribing them.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.170
Show me what you're made of, little ones.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:16.170
Let's see what you can do!

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:20.250
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:21.960
Here are the coagulation factors!

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:23.170
Okay!

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.000
"BOOM"

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.790
Primary Platelet blood clot!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.000
Ah, impressive clumping.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.790
You're compensating for what you lack
in numbers with your technique.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.380
Not only that, but look at that total stability.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.250
I don't know if it's your thirst
for a gold medal or just plain guts...

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.710
Right!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.380
All righty!

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:44.880
Here! The last of the coagulation factors!

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.120
--Thanks!
--Sure!

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.750
All right, now we can...

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.540
"SLIP"

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.710
What the...

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.790
O-Oh no! Our precious coagulation factor!

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.790
Come back here!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:06.960
Backward Cap!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:10.170
"SNAP"

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:13.120
I did it! I got it!

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:17.500
Everybody! We're going to do
that clumping move now!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:22.250
But that formation is so hard,
we've never managed to do it even once!

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.500
Don't worry!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.830
I'm sure we can make it this time...

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.460
...if we all work together as one!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.460
O-Okay!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:35.670
Go!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.170
Now, that's an incredible super skill!

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.790
Backward Cap! I'm coming!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.920
Don't let go!

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.790
Hold onto my hand and the coagulation factor!

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:52.750
Okay!

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:56.040
It's all good! Don't worry, Leader!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:59.210
I'm not letting go,
I know for sure that I won't ever let go!

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:02.670
That's the spirit, Backward Cap!
All your training is paying off now!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:05.210
You've gained a little strength
in those arms, huh?

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.710
Good for you!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:16.580
Excellent! What amazing cohesion!
Look at you, rising to the occasion!

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:20.380
To think that even I'm floored
by your growth as your master!

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.580
You little ones are truly something else!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:26.790
My little ones!

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:30.380
Thanks to your efforts, we were able to keep
today's hemorrhage from escalating,

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.920
and we've stopped the bleeding!

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:34.540
Good job! I commend you for your hard work!

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.670
Yes, Master!

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:39.540
But I can't make up my mind about something.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:43.670
Who it is that I should award
the gold medal to, you know?

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:44.830
And why is that?

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:48.750
Because although it's true that Backward Cap
mustered her courage and came up clutch for us,

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:54.460
still, she was too sluggish before that,
during clotting! You have to try harder, okay?

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.250
Leader, you displayed some impressive
supervision skills,

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:02.420
but it was also you who dropped
the coagulation factor! A careless mistake!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:03.960
"HMM"

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.290
You all worked very hard,

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:13.540
but it's not like I saw an ultra-good kid
who stood head and shoulders above the rest.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:17.000
So, today I have no choice but to...

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.420
...give you all a gold medal!

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:22.380
"CLATTER"
"CLANG"
...give you all a gold medal!

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.420
"CLATTER"
"CLANG"
Master!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:28.460
"YAY"
Yay! Yay!

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.420
Backward Cap...

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.790
You really came through for us today!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:36.830
It was your efforts that brought
everyone else together as one!

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.540
Master!

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.500
Since you've always been twice
as weak as the others,

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:46.290
I always worried if you'd make it or not.
But now, you've set my mind at ease.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:51.000
Backward Cap, as an apprentice,
you're my pride and joy!

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.540
--Master! Master!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.540
--Hey you!
--Master! Master!

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.920
That's a relief.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:21:01.420
I had no clue how that was going to turn out,
but it looks like I worried too much.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:04.960
Backward Cap, not only do you
have a positive attitude,

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:08.710
but you also have great friends
and a great master.

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:12.420
There was no way that you wouldn't
find a way to overcome that jam!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:16.500
Always cherish the memory of today,
as well as that gold medal.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.960
Backward Cap--

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:24.290
Gold medal! Gold medal!
Gold medal! Gold medal!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.790
Master!

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:30.710
See you, little ones!
Do your best next time, too!

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:33.000
Okay!

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:06.330
--All right! All right! All right!

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:10.750
--Here are more blood cells for the clot!
--All right! All right! All right!

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:14.210
White Blood Cell! Good job!

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:17.290
Oh, right. So, you're safe
and sound. That's good.

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:22.290
Huh? You have an ever-so-slightly hurt look
on your face. Are you all right?

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:24.960
Sure. Hey, it's nothing.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:28.500
The mood swings this guy goes through
over the most trivial stuff!

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.380
Just because he got a little trampled on.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.250
Trampled on?

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.500
Well, I'm sure it wasn't on purpose, so...

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.120
Who was it that trampled on you?

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:36.920
Well, actually...

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:37.670
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"

00:23:37.670 --> 00:23:39.290
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
Memory Cell did mention something.

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:40.120
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
What did he say?

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:41.920
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
That the world's going to end
for sure this time.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:43.830
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
He has a feeling that it may
or may not happen.

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:44.750
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
So, which is it?

00:23:44.750 --> 00:23:46.500
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
Next episode of <i>Cells at Work!!</i>,

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:46.920
"NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW"
"Acquired Immunity/Peyer's Patch."

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:48.920
"EPISODE 2:
ACQUIRED IMMUNITY/PEYER'S PATCH"
"Acquired Immunity/Peyer's Patch."

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:51.380
"EPISODE 2:
ACQUIRED IMMUNITY/PEYER'S PATCH"
Work hard, everyday!

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.000
